digraph ReasoningTree {
  rankdir="TB";
  "Icapability" [label="(0,0,0) deduction: Given that CP semiconducting capability depends on long-range delocalization and that CP single crystals are an ideal platform for peak performance and structure–property studies, therefore improving CP thin-film crystallinity toward single-crystal-like order is important for CP electronics."];
  "Ievidence" [label="(0,0,0) deduction: Given that nano-CMDO is introduced for assembling CPs into single-crystal thin films and that nano-CMDO offers a promising non-epitaxial avenue for CP single-crystal growth, therefore nano-CMDO is a credible proposed route for CP single-crystal thin-film growth."];
  "Inano" [label="(0,0,0) If a nanoconfined capacitor can impose a well-defined perpendicular electric field and steric/chemical confinement, then it can provide nanoscopic control over dipole orientation and molecular conformation."];
  "Ineed" [label="(0,0,0) If CP applications demand high-performance thin-film electronics, then improving thin-film crystallinity toward single-crystal-like order is a key materials goal."];
  "Iopportunity" [label="(0,0,0) abduction: Given that thin-film crystallization lacks precise control and background knowledge that dipoles can modulate π–π stacking energetics to lower barriers, therefore dipole-mediated energy-landscape modulation is a plausible opportunity to enable single-crystal thin films."];
  "Iproblem" [label="(0,0,0) induction: Given that CP single-crystal manufacturing faces an energetic-preference vs entropic-cost contradiction and that thin-film 2D constraints disrupt favorable π–π stacking, therefore the common problem is lack of precise control of ordering/crystallization in CP thin films."];
  "Ipromise" [label="(0,0,0) deduction: Given that nano-CMDO is a plausible solution strategy and that nano-CMDO offers a promising non-epitaxial avenue for CP single-crystal growth, therefore pursuing nano-CMDO is justified as a promising non-epitaxial route."];
  "Iproposal" [label="(0,0,0) abduction: Given the need to overcome thin-film crystallization-control problems and background knowledge that a nano-CMDO strategy is explicitly proposed for assembling CPs into single-crystal thin films, therefore adopting nano-CMDO is a plausible best-explanation solution strategy."];
  "Isolution" [label="(0,0,0) abduction: Given the thin-film crystallization-control problem and background knowledge that dipoles can accelerate nucleation via ordered initial states, therefore dipole-based control is a plausible mechanism to enable improved crystal growth."];
  "Ithermo" [label="(0,0,0) deduction: Given that molecular dipoles exist in CPs and that dipoles can modulate π–π stacking energetics to lower the barrier toward a single-crystal state, therefore dipoles provide a thermodynamic lever to reduce the barrier to single-crystal ordering."];
  "N12S" [label="(12,0,0) Currently achieving equilibrium between localized molecular rotations and global chain alignment to precisely modulate thin-film crystallization remains elusive."];
  "N13S" [label="(13,0,0) Currently a universal nanoconfined molecular-dipole orienting (nano-CMDO) strategy is introduced to assemble CPs into single-crystal thin films."];
  "N14S" [label="(14,0,0) Currently a spatial-electrostatic nanoconfined capacitor is designed where a perpendicular electric field rotates backbones via dipoles, and alkyl-modified plates regulate side chains."];
  "N19S" [label="(19,0,0) Currently nano-CMDO offers a promising non-epitaxial avenue for CP single-crystal growth."];
  "N1S" [label="(1,0,0) Currently conjugated polymers (CPs) are increasingly important for wearable, biocompatible, and neuromorphic thin-film electronics."];
  "N2S" [label="(2,0,0) Currently CP semiconducting capability depends on long-range delocalization of electronic wavefunctions across polymer chains."];
  "N3S" [label="(3,0,0) Currently CP single crystals (coplanar conformation, low energetic disorder, high mobility) are an ideal platform for peak performance and structure–property studies."];
  "N4S" [label="(4,0,0) Currently manufacturing CP single crystals is significantly challenging due to an energetic-preference vs entropic-cost contradiction in ordering polymer chains."];
  "N5S" [label="(5,0,0) Currently in thin films, 2D constraints and disruption of π–π stacking further exacerbate difficulty of forming the energetically favorable crystalline state."];
  "N6S" [label="(6,0,0) Currently electronegativity differences in CPs create localized molecular dipoles (asymmetric electron distribution)."];
  "N7S" [label="(7,0,0) Currently molecular dipoles can modulate the π–π stacking energy landscape and lower the energy barrier toward a single-crystal state."];
  "N8S" [label="(8,0,0) Currently molecular dipoles can accelerate nucleation by fostering highly ordered initial states and thus promote uniform/rapid crystal growth."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Develop and evaluate a universal nano-CMDO strategy using a spatial-electrostatic nanoconfined capacitor to orient molecular dipoles, rotate conjugated-polymer backbones, regulate side chains, and promote assembly of conjugated polymers into single-crystal thin films for high-performance organic electronics.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When a materials-performance need, a crystallization-control problem, mechanistic dipole-based opportunities, and a concrete nanoconfined capacitor implementation converge, they jointly motivate developing and evaluating a proposed thin-film crystallization strategy rather than proving it a priori."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) The described spatial-electrostatic nanoconfined capacitor provides a concrete implementation of the nanoconfined-capacitor design direction, using a perpendicular electric field to rotate backbones through dipoles and alkyl-modified plates to regulate side chains."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) Because conjugated polymers contain localized molecular dipoles and molecular dipoles can modulate the π–π stacking energy landscape to lower the barrier toward a single-crystal state, dipole-oriented strategies are plausible thermodynamic levers for favoring ordered stacking."];
  "R16" [label="(0,0,0) The need to improve conjugated-polymer thin-film crystallinity, together with the promise of nano-CMDO as a non-epitaxial route for single-crystal growth, supports proposing to develop and evaluate nano-CMDO for high-performance CP thin-film electronics."];
  "R9" [label="(0,0,0) Because precise equilibrium between localized molecular rotations and global chain alignment remains elusive, a nanoconfined capacitor capable of imposing a perpendicular electric field and steric/chemical confinement is a plausible design direction for nanoscopic dipole-orientation and molecular-conformation control."];
  "N2S" -> "Icapability" [label="deduction-case"];
  "N3S" -> "Icapability" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "Icapability" -> "Ineed" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "N1S" -> "Ineed" [label="deduction-case"];
